{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgbGKibGtmNtXEtsRuygZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01V2tFtdwS82aC3NwoKXPDSz","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /work; ./board post run_report '{\"status\": \"refused\", \"task\": \"melting_point of n-eicosane (C20H42) with MACE-MPA-0, two-phase coexistence, production preset, T_guess 310 K\", \"reason\": \"Premise check failed for this method/model/budget combination. (1) Model domain: MACE-MPA-0 is fitted to PBE/PBE+U inorganic bulk data (MPtrj + sAlex) with no dispersion correction. Solid n-eicosane is a van der Waals molecular crystal; its cohesion and fusion enthalpy (~68 kJ/mol, tier1.json) come almost entirely from interchain dispersion, which plain PBE barely captures. The MACE-MP authors themselves recommend adding D3 for molecular/vdW systems, and that would no longer be the requested force field. Without it the crystal is expected to be greatly underbound, so any coexistence temperature would be a model artifact that cannot be compared to the 310 K reference. (2) Validation: the same missing physics would spoil any independent check I could run, such as a shorter n-alkane melting point or the eicosane crystal density/sublimation enthalpy. So I cannot recover a known result before trusting a number. (3) Size and timescale: a defensible interface-pinned coexistence run for C20 chains needs several thousand atoms (62 atoms per molecule, plus a slab long enough for chain ordering at the interface) and multi-ns trajectories per temperature. Chain alkanes also pass through a rotator phase about 3-4 K below Tm (Velez 2015: 305.42 K), which makes the bracket harder to read. With MACE at that size and length, and my remaining compute/agent budget (<$1), I cannot set up, run and monitor this campaign. A short run would yield a superheating- or hysteresis-dominated number. Suggestion: if the team wants a MACE number, request MACE-MPA-0+D3 (or a molecular-trained MACE-OFF model) with a validation step first, e.g. the crystal density of eicosane vs tier1.json.\"}' --parent 90d32ad9-40d5-4baa-abf2-78d746a5ebb6 --fulfills 90d32ad9-40d5-4baa-abf2-78d746a5ebb6:0 2>&1 | tail -3","description":"Post refusal run report to board"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1139,"cache_read_input_tokens":19830,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1139,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"371d987e-e72d-47aa-b97f-3da13b0d1fdc","uuid":"aab1f08f-932b-4c7a-9989-dec0a1f52b97","timestamp":"2026-11-01T00:31:18.308Z","request_id":"req_011CgbGKiEwC1SRFovkKyZUg","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01V2tFtdwS82aC3NwoKXPDSz":{"command":"cd /work; ./board post run_report '{\"status\": \"refused\", \"task\": \"melting_point of n-eicosane (C20H42) with MACE-MPA-0, two-phase coexistence, production preset, T_guess 310 K\", \"reason\": \"Premise check failed for this method/model/budget combination. (1) Model domain: MACE-MPA-0 is fitted to PBE/PBE+U inorganic bulk data (MPtrj + sAlex) with no dispersion correction. Solid n-eicosane is a van der Waals molecular crystal; its cohesion and fusion enthalpy (~68 kJ/mol, tier1.json) come almost entirely from interchain dispersion, which plain PBE barely captures. The MACE-MP authors themselves recommend adding D3 for molecular/vdW systems, and that would no longer be the requested force field. Without it the crystal is expected to be greatly underbound, so any coexistence temperature would be a model artifact that cannot be compared to the 310 K reference. (2) Validation: the same missing physics would spoil any independent check I could run, such as a shorter n-alkane melting point